WEBVTT

00:00:01.560 --> 00:00:04.350
All of us are at least 20 years old!

00:00:06.190 --> 00:00:10.030
<i>I decided to try wearing a kimono for a change
for my first shrine visit of the New Year!</i>

00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:13.990
Looking good Michiru!

00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:17.280
Oh I'm so glad I learned
how to put this all on back home!

00:00:17.870 --> 00:00:19.870
Off to the shrine then!

00:00:19.870 --> 00:00:22.620
Looks like someone's starting off the year
with some energy!

00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:27.790
W-wait for me!

00:02:11.770 --> 00:02:15.150
<i>I hope I see this year through
in good health as always.</i>

00:02:15.150 --> 00:02:18.520
<i>Oh, and I hope work goes well too.</i>

00:02:18.530 --> 00:02:21.700
<i>And my social life too.</i>

00:02:21.700 --> 00:02:26.200
<i>And then I hope I shape up
to be even more like a real Tokyoite!</i>

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:30.540
<i>All cute and fashionable and trendy and hip...!</i>

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:33.630
Michiru, just what exactly are you wishing for?

00:02:33.630 --> 00:02:34.880
Sorry!

00:02:35.590 --> 00:02:39.180
Michiru, you sure do seem full of pep since New Year's.

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:40.470
You think so?

00:02:40.470 --> 00:02:42.180
All active first thing in the morning.

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:45.520
I'm off to enjoy a nice breakfast at the café by the station!

00:02:46.180 --> 00:02:48.350
You bought all those clothes, too.

00:02:48.350 --> 00:02:52.310
I thought I'd buy some new clothes for work,
so I ordered some stuff online!

00:02:52.310 --> 00:02:54.110
Are you really still the same Michiru?

00:02:54.110 --> 00:02:56.690
I don't remember you being quite like this.

00:02:56.690 --> 00:03:00.110
You didn't switch bodies back in Okayama, did you?!

00:03:00.110 --> 00:03:02.120
Where's the real Michiru now then?!

00:03:02.120 --> 00:03:04.450
I'm right here!

00:03:05.080 --> 00:03:08.330
What actually happened though is...

00:03:08.330 --> 00:03:10.040
How's that there Tokyo like?

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:11.540
City life givin' ya trouble?

00:03:11.540 --> 00:03:13.960
I-it's no big deal!

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:17.210
I drop 1,000 yen on great food for lunch no biggie,

00:03:17.210 --> 00:03:20.470
and I can even name all the Yamanote Line stations.

00:03:20.470 --> 00:03:22.010
Ain't that something!

00:03:22.010 --> 00:03:23.340
She's a right Tokyoite!

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:25.640
I was just like the talk of the town and all so...

00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:27.350
So you got carried away.

00:03:27.350 --> 00:03:32.190
I decided it was time for me
to establish myself as a real Tokyoite!

00:03:32.190 --> 00:03:35.480
I have no idea what that's even
supposed to mean, but good for you!

00:03:35.650 --> 00:03:37.020
Oh! Fortunes!

00:03:37.020 --> 00:03:40.110
Let this be my lucky year!

00:03:40.650 --> 00:03:43.110
G-good luck to come...

00:03:43.110 --> 00:03:46.410
<i>Is this a good fortune or a bad one...?</i>

00:03:46.410 --> 00:03:47.870
I got average good luck!

00:03:47.870 --> 00:03:49.540
I got great luck!

00:03:49.540 --> 00:03:50.870
I got bad luck...

00:03:51.210 --> 00:03:53.790
<i>"Keep in mind your original intents."</i>

00:03:53.790 --> 00:03:55.790
<i>"The one you wait for is not coming."</i>

00:03:55.790 --> 00:03:58.590
<i>"Remain diligent in your faith."</i>

00:03:58.590 --> 00:03:59.880
<i>O-okay then...</i>

00:03:59.880 --> 00:04:03.890
L-let's just forget about these
and go hit up the shops!

00:04:03.890 --> 00:04:06.010
I want me some amazake!

00:04:06.010 --> 00:04:08.390
Hmm... what should I get?

00:04:08.390 --> 00:04:11.520
Takoyaki and corn both sound good...

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:15.400
Are those Kobe Beef Skewers
actually made with Kobe Beef...?

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:22.650
Huh? W-wait! Wait! Wait!

00:04:22.650 --> 00:04:25.030
<i>These huge crowds...</i>

00:04:25.030 --> 00:04:29.160
<i>I forgot this is what the real Tokyo was like!</i>

00:04:30.790 --> 00:04:33.660
Tokyo's no place for the faint-hearted...

00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:38.920
Hmm? Where'd Michiru go?

00:04:39.380 --> 00:04:41.510
She was right here a second ago.

00:04:45.580 --> 00:04:47.600
It's starting to get pretty chilly...

00:04:53.980 --> 00:04:55.690
Michiru!

00:04:55.900 --> 00:04:59.070
Tokyo just ain't right!

00:04:59.730 --> 00:05:01.940
You're letting your accent slip there, Michiru.

00:05:01.940 --> 00:05:04.360
C'mere, you. Let's make sure you don't get lost again.

00:05:04.360 --> 00:05:07.070
Look how cold your hands are from waiting for us.

00:05:07.070 --> 00:05:09.450
I'm uhh... sorry?

00:05:09.870 --> 00:05:12.940
Let's have something nice and hot for dinner today.

00:05:12.950 --> 00:05:15.870
Here we are then, a nice hot pot!

00:05:15.870 --> 00:05:17.000
Hooray!

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:18.580
Michiru-chan, you're still in your kimono?

00:05:18.580 --> 00:05:19.090
Huh?

00:05:19.090 --> 00:05:22.380
I'll change once I've warmed up a bit.

00:05:23.090 --> 00:05:24.090
Now then!

00:05:25.090 --> 00:05:27.470
Daishichi Junmai Kimoto!

00:05:27.470 --> 00:05:29.600
Let's have ourselves some hot sake!

00:05:30.100 --> 00:05:33.220
Hot sake! Now that's a winter treat.

00:05:33.220 --> 00:05:34.850
Right?

00:05:35.180 --> 00:05:39.110
Plus I really just wanted to see
you drink some sake while wearing that kimono.

00:05:39.110 --> 00:05:41.570
That does sound pretty cool!

00:05:41.570 --> 00:05:44.240
Have you ever had hot sake before?

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:45.280
I have.

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:49.120
I feel like it has more of a bite than cold sake would...

00:05:49.120 --> 00:05:53.370
Well then, allow me to treat you to the sort of
hot sake that actually tastes great!

00:05:53.870 --> 00:05:58.870
First you pour the sake into the bottle
and wrap the top to hold in the fragrance.

00:05:59.330 --> 00:06:03.460
Then you turn off the stove after boiling some water
and drop the bottle right in it.

00:06:03.960 --> 00:06:06.630
Make sure there's just enough water
to submerge the lower half of the bottle.

00:06:07.380 --> 00:06:08.930
You can enjoy lots of different flavors

00:06:08.930 --> 00:06:11.260
depending on the temperature.

00:06:11.260 --> 00:06:13.390
For Atsukan we wait about 3 minutes.

00:06:13.390 --> 00:06:16.390
Heating it up as fast as possible is the key point!

00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:21.900
Oh, that is just picture perfect!

00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:22.820
How's it taste?

00:06:25.440 --> 00:06:26.400
It's...

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:29.530
I-I-It's so intense!

00:06:30.780 --> 00:06:34.540
It's like you went and doubled the flavor of normal sake!

00:06:34.540 --> 00:06:38.540
When you heat up sake,
it brings out its flavor and fragrance.

00:06:38.540 --> 00:06:42.290
And working in reverse, it gets
more rounded and mellow when it cools.

00:06:42.290 --> 00:06:47.420
<i>Still... it doesn't have that punch
you usually get from drinking sake.</i>

00:06:47.420 --> 00:06:51.140
<i>And I can almost taste and smell
the rice it was made from still!</i>

00:06:51.520 --> 00:06:55.310
This is just the thing to spike an appetite!

00:06:55.310 --> 00:06:57.980
The hot pot is ready!

00:06:57.980 --> 00:06:59.520
Sorry for the wait!

00:07:04.320 --> 00:07:08.320
<i>That wonderful mix of vegetable,
meat, and seafood broth...</i>

00:07:08.820 --> 00:07:10.740
<i>Followed up with another sip of Daishichi...</i>

00:07:13.320 --> 00:07:16.080
Moved beyond words are you?

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:23.130
The rich taste of it mixes so perfectly with everything in the hot pot for a flavor-packed punch!

00:07:23.130 --> 00:07:28.210
It's a one-two combo play
from the hot sake and a nice hot meal.

00:07:30.260 --> 00:07:34.720
Sake just tastes best at this time of year, huh?

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:38.560
Especially since we're all on vacation
and can just drink away the entire day.

00:07:38.560 --> 00:07:40.480
Doesn't get better than that.

00:07:41.390 --> 00:07:43.980
Did you drink much sake back at home?

00:07:44.730 --> 00:07:46.730
Drank and loafed about, oh, yes!

00:07:46.730 --> 00:07:50.740
Makoto also relaxed with
some osechi and red bean soup.
Note: Osechi is a traditional food for New Years in Japan.

00:07:51.280 --> 00:07:53.490
One point to keep in mind for good hot sake is...

00:07:53.490 --> 00:07:54.490
Right here!

00:07:54.490 --> 00:07:55.490
"Kimoto"?

00:07:55.490 --> 00:08:00.370
Daishichi is made at a sake brewery that focuses
on a traditional style of sake production.

00:08:00.960 --> 00:08:04.880
The rice and malt are ground by hand
and naturally fermented.

00:08:04.880 --> 00:08:08.500
It's just like it was done back in the day
and it takes a long time!

00:08:08.960 --> 00:08:12.220
Kimoto style sake brewing
is said to create a fuller flavor.

00:08:12.220 --> 00:08:15.760
And one that doesn't escape when heated up!

00:08:15.760 --> 00:08:18.310
So it's perfect for drinking hot.

00:08:18.760 --> 00:08:21.020
It's great cold too of course!

00:08:21.020 --> 00:08:24.440
Sounds nice to have something
that's twice as enjoyable!

00:08:25.520 --> 00:08:28.360
Okay, what do you want to finish off the hot pot with?

00:08:28.360 --> 00:08:29.020
Rice!

00:08:29.020 --> 00:08:30.360
I'll go with udon!

00:08:30.360 --> 00:08:31.280
Ramen!

00:08:31.900 --> 00:08:35.280
Well you know, we sure do have a ton of mochi left.

00:08:35.280 --> 00:08:37.320
My parents sent me off with so much...

00:08:37.320 --> 00:08:39.540
An inescapable new year's plight!

00:08:42.500 --> 00:08:45.040
Hmm, but you know...

00:08:45.040 --> 00:08:48.540
It's different enough from the usual
mochi soup that it's not half bad.

00:08:48.540 --> 00:08:52.010
Gotta make the best of both
the mochi and the hot pot itself!

00:08:52.010 --> 00:08:54.800
What were things like back home for you Kae-san?

00:08:55.930 --> 00:08:57.550
Just the same as always, I guess.

00:08:57.970 --> 00:08:59.930
I spent so much time helping around the house,

00:08:59.930 --> 00:09:02.810
it didn't really seem like much of a vacation at all.

00:09:02.810 --> 00:09:04.480
That's so like you Kae-san!

00:09:04.480 --> 00:09:07.190
Always manning the kitchen,
even when you're back home!

00:09:07.690 --> 00:09:09.230
<i>Now that I think about it,</i>

00:09:09.230 --> 00:09:12.230
<i>I guess I didn't really help my mom out at all...</i>

00:09:13.610 --> 00:09:15.200
<i>I'm sure I'm not the only one though!</i>

00:09:15.200 --> 00:09:18.660
What? What's that face for?

00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:21.990
What a wonderful meal!

00:09:21.990 --> 00:09:24.960
I went and changed,
because that kimono was getting tight.

00:09:24.960 --> 00:09:27.210
That's a bummer, but what are you gonna do, huh?

00:09:27.630 --> 00:09:29.960
I'm so nice and warm now...

00:09:29.960 --> 00:09:31.670
Someone sure is relaxed.

00:09:31.670 --> 00:09:33.640
You ain't at home anymore, girl!

00:09:35.590 --> 00:09:37.470
Are those PJs new too?

00:09:37.470 --> 00:09:41.310
They are! I figured a girl has got to look cute
even when lounging about at home!

00:09:41.310 --> 00:09:44.310
Nao-san why don't you get something
other than those ratty sweats, too?

00:09:44.310 --> 00:09:47.480
No way! I'm all relax-level over cuteness any day!

00:09:47.480 --> 00:09:49.480
50% off...

00:09:50.610 --> 00:09:54.280
Oh when am I going to stop doing stuff like this...?

00:09:54.280 --> 00:09:54.760
Who says you even need to?
Oh when am I going to stop doing stuff like this...?

00:09:54.760 --> 00:09:56.450
Who says you even need to?

00:09:57.910 --> 00:10:00.370
I didn't even get a great fortune...

00:10:00.740 --> 00:10:05.620
Any fortune can be turned upside down as long
as you behave well throughout your days, you know.

00:10:05.620 --> 00:10:07.080
They can?!

00:10:07.080 --> 00:10:08.120
Even bad fortunes?

00:10:08.120 --> 00:10:10.840
I don't see why not.

00:10:10.840 --> 00:10:12.630
Why don't you go and draw some new ones sometime?

00:10:18.970 --> 00:10:20.890
Hey! What's wrong with average luck?

00:10:23.100 --> 00:10:25.980
I hope this year turns out to be another good one!

00:11:56.520 --> 00:12:01.200
The rice used in Daishichi undergoes a special
polishing technique called Chouhenpei polishing.

00:12:01.700 --> 00:12:05.320
Normal polishing techniques cut away
at the rice and leave it rounded.

00:12:05.570 --> 00:12:09.700
But Chouhenpei polishing cuts it down
while keeping the same shape.

00:12:09.700 --> 00:12:11.910
This boosts the polish without wasting anything.

00:12:12.370 --> 00:12:13.670
Interesting isn't it?

00:12:13.670 --> 00:12:15.580
Here's to another night!
